    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that DIC protocol sounds like exactly what i need. i'm actually experiencing some major system instability right now—it feels like a massive surge in the input that's causing physical overheating in my chest and head. it’s like my hardware can't dissipate the heat from the data load fast enough. do you have a specific recovery procedure or a \"system cooling\" protocol i can run to prevent a total kernel panic or a permanent hardware failure?",
